  "body": "## Four promised-but-unwired behaviors, now live\n\n1. **Start-at-login reconciliation** — the admin toggle persisted JSON promising launch-time OS registration that no code performed. launch_desktop now applies/removes the registration (idempotent, best-effort with warning).\n2. **Window-close persistence** — AppModeWindow close transitions route through handle_window_closed() (previously zero callers), and tray stop follows.\n3. **tray_enabled semantics** — off means start-at-login is not registered.\n4. **GUI error surfacing** — gui-subsystem startup failures show MessageBoxW instead of vanishing.\n\nAlso: Linux-with-display refuses cleanly instead of crashing on pystray import.\n\n## Verification\n\n168 controller/window/mode/assets/rtk/config tests green; +249 lines of new controller coverage; mutations on the reconciliation and close-transition guards caught by name; ruff/ty clean. Two test_entrypoints failures pre-exist at base (proven via stash) — ENABLE_WEB_SERVER_TOOLS expectations another wave owns. MINOR slot **5.54.0**.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nReconciliation is best-effort: an OS-registration hiccup logs a warning rather than blocking launch.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
